# Account, not wallet

In all **user-facing** copy (iMessage, web UI, API error messages shown to users, soul/prompts, landing pages), call the user's iStonk smart account an **Account**. Never say "wallet" to the user.

## Prefer

- "your iStonk account"
- "set up your account" / "connect your account"
- "from your account" / "in your account"
- "Open your account" / "Account" in nav
- Matchers should accept both `account` and legacy `wallet` phrasing from users

## Keep as code / infra (do not rename for this rule)

- Identifiers: `WalletAdapter`, `EmbeddedWallet`, `walletAddress`, `kind: "wallet"`, `WalletInfo`, `api.wallet()`, component names like `Wallet()`
- Routes and APIs: `/wallet/connect`, `/api/app/stonks/wallet`, `/#wallet` anchors
- DB columns, CDP Portal product names ("Embedded Wallet" in Coinbase docs)
- On-chain slang in internal comments when referring to EOAs generally is fine; product copy is not

## When writing new copy

If you catch yourself typing "wallet" for something the user sees, rewrite to **account** before shipping.
